course: dictionary
lesson: 940
title: Blob: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one is meant. «She put a blob of paint on the page» tells you a blob is a small lump of thick colour.
explain: «Octopuses squirt ink to make a fake blob while they jet away.» Here a blob is a shape that is hard to see clearly, because the ink is there to hide the octopus. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? A lump of jelly would not make sense here, but a hard-to-see shape does.
explain: Blob can also be a verb, and then it is informal, so you will hear it in chatty speech more than in books. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A blob is a small, round lump of a thick liquid, like paint, glue or jam.
fact: A blob can also be a shape or thing that is hard to see clearly, with no clear outline.
fact: As a verb, blob is informal and means to put small lumps of something somewhere.
fact: «A blob of cream» means a small round lump of cream.
fact: In 1928 Alexander Fleming saw «a blob of mould» on a dish of germs, and the germs around it had died.
exercise: «She put a blob of glue on the card.» What is a blob here? | A shape that is hard to see clearly | *A small round lump of thick glue | A fast little boat | A piece of chewy sweet
exercise: «In the dark we could only see a grey blob moving near the tree.» What does blob mean? | A tasty pudding | *A shape that is hard to see clearly | A lump of cheese | A loud noise
exercise: «Sam will blob a little paint onto the page.» What does blob mean here? | *To put small lumps of paint somewhere | To wash the paint off | To lose the paint | To paint a whole wall
test: «The octopus squirted ink to make a fake blob.» Which meaning fits best? | A sort of fish dinner | *A shape that is hard to see clearly, hidden in the ink | A small round lump of jam | The end of a long story
test: «Pass me a blob of cream for my pudding.» Which meaning fits best? | To hide something under a blanket | A shape with no clear outline in the dark | A cold, wet day | *A small round lump of thick cream
exam: Which sentence uses blob as an informal verb? | *Ella will blob a little glue on each corner of the card. | Octopuses squirt ink to hide. | The cook put a blob of cream on top. | The strange blob drifted across the sky.
